cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LaraIoT-App in your research, thesis, or benchmarking projects, please cite it as follows."
type: software
title: "LaraIoT-App: A Containerized Demonstration Application Using the LaraIoT Laravel Package"
abstract: >-
  LaraIoT-App is a containerized demonstration application illustrating
  how the LaraIoT Laravel package (danpopa/laraiot) can be used to build
  web applications for monitoring and controlling IoT devices.
  It provides a Docker-based environment integrating MQTT communication,
  device state persistence in MariaDB, background MQTT message processing,
  and a web interface built with Vue.js and Inertia.
  The application supports two alternative mechanisms for updating data
  in the web interface: periodic HTTP polling and WebSockets through
  Laravel Reverb. It provides a practical starting point for developers
  and a reference implementation for exploring and comparing these
  mechanisms in controlled IoT environments.
  LaraIoT-App is intended for research, education, and prototyping.
  Security hardening is outside its scope, and additional safeguards
  are required before deployment in production environments.
repository-code: "https://github.com/danielpopa26/laraiot-app"
